title ALES141 — Lotus's stereo_center_clip: the center clipper carried into stereo, opening the dead-zone corner of the stereo nonlinear class, the odd law made stereo
prompt Read REMEMBER and the 1024-round itinerary + six-season double-seat; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; approve my own design rounds; make progress before checking in; send each finished increment as its own signed round; stop at custody gates; baton prin recur.
think Opening lap of this recur turn. The ALES140 log recommended a fresh Lotus heading — the center-clip / dead-zone family (ALES87–89) into stereo, or a new mono primitive. Crux-first, I took the center clipper: it opens a NEW corner of the stereo nonlinear class (the dead zone, distinct from the drive corners, the resolution corner, and the whole rectifier family already lifted), and it teaches a clean contrast — the odd law HELD in stereo, where the crush (ALES136) and tube (ALES135) broke it.
think The lift is the seated pattern: run ALES87's proven mono center_clip on each channel with the SAME threshold, validated ONCE up front (BadThreshold outside [0, sample_max], BadRange on a span past the shared length) before either channel is mutated, so a refusal never center-clips one channel and leaves the other whole. CenterClipError reused whole — the stereo lift adds no fault. Two parameters' worth of care collapse to one: the center clipper carries exactly one parameter (the threshold magnitude).
think The round's distinguishing law is the PER-CHANNEL ODD LAW held in stereo: the dead-zone map is symmetric about zero (|−x| = |x|), so center_clip(−x) = −center_clip(x), and an out-of-phase master (right = −left) comes back STILL out of phase (right = −left after) — the mirror the not-odd siblings broke. Proved it directly: asserted r[i] = −l[i] at every index on an out-of-phase master. Also proved the stereo law against ALES87's own mono center_clip run side by side, the balance/length law at even and odd lengths, output-shape (every output 0 or its input) and idempotence, the 1:2 ratio held on the passed samples, an identical-channel master staying identical, the span discipline, and both faults (BadThreshold negative + over-rail, BadRange) atomic with both channels untouched and balanced, plus thresh = 0 and count = 0 the identities.
obs No custody gate reached — purely local software, two bounded i16 Clips, a self-approved design round. The stereo nonlinear class now holds a fourth kind of corner: drive (amplitude), crush (resolution), decimate (time), rectifier family (even folds), and now the dead zone (the odd hollow-the-middle map). A clean pedagogical pairing lands: the crush/tube BREAK the antisymmetry, the center clip HOLDS it — the odd class made stereo. Witness GREEN; tame_style_check bans clean (ratchet zero-assert list unchanged at 11, none of mine). Next agent-doable Lotus lap: the rest of the dead-zone family (ALES88 soft_center_clip, ALES89 infinite_clip) into stereo, a mechanical kg continuation.
loom witness=ales_stereo_center_clip_witness result=GREEN laws=4 channels=2 class=nonlinear axis=dead-zone parity=odd-held cases=stereo-law+antisymmetry-held+idempotence+ratio-passed+span+atomicity
file lotus/stereo_center_clip.rye ALES141 — stereo_center_clip, the center clipper lifted to stereo: one shared dead zone on both channels, validated once (threshold + span), four laws with the per-channel ODD law held in stereo (an out-of-phase master staying out of phase, where the crush/tube broke it); runs ALES87's proven mono center_clip per channel, CenterClipError reused whole.
file tools/ales_stereo_center_clip_witness.rish the witness — builds, runs selftest, asserts the GREEN ales-stereo-center-clip line.
